{{!-- LAYOUT SELECTION — four boolean flags, exactly one truthy per call:
        layoutGrid="true"       2-up cards
        layoutList="true"       single-column list rows
        layoutRhythm="true"     1-2-1 cadence (full-width row, then a pair,
                                 repeating)
        layoutCinematic="true"  one big centered hero card per row
      None passed → falls back to @custom.posts_layout (theme setting).

      Booleans, not a single layout="grid"/"list"/... string, because
      Ghost's Handlebars has no eq/string-compare helper and themes cannot
      register custom helpers (see the filter-string note further down
      this comment for the same constraint) — an if-block can only test
      one variable's truthiness, never "does this string equal X", so a
      single multi-value param can't be routed to 4 different outcomes.
      One boolean per option is the only helper-free mechanism that works.

      itemContent="outside" — optional, orthogonal to the 4 flags above.
      Selects whether card copy (category/title/testimonial/etc) sits
      overlaid inside the image or as a separate block below/beside it.
      Checked with a truthy if-block (same eq-less constraint as the
      layout flags above — Ghost's Handlebars can't compare string values),
      so any non-empty value reads as "outside"; the literal text "inside"
      would ALSO be truthy and still mean outside. To get a layout's own
      default, omit the param entirely.

        layoutGrid / layoutRhythm / layoutCinematic — default is INSIDE
        (overlaid). itemContent="outside" flips to outside/beside.
        layoutList — default is INSIDE (overlaid) too.
        itemContent="outside" flips to outside/beside (list's original
        look: image left, copy in a separate block to the right).

      itemContent="outside" therefore means OUTSIDE in every layout
      (2026-08-30). It used to be defined as "flip away from this layout's
      default", which for layoutList inverted the word: passing "outside"
      produced the overlaid INSIDE style and omitting it gave outside —
      the opposite of every other layout and of the param's own name.
      Both list styles already existed in CSS (bare
      [data-posts-layout='list'] is beside/outside, plus a full
      [data-item-content='inside'] block for overlaid), so only this
      mapping changed, not the styling.

      Only 3 of the resulting 8 combinations have CSS today:
        layoutGrid + itemContent="outside"
        layoutRhythm + itemContent="outside"
        layoutList (omitted → inside/overlaid, and "outside" → beside;
                    both are styled)
      layoutCinematic + itemContent="outside" has no CSS yet — falls
      through to unstyled base .posts-grid rules if used.

      Example (call-site syntax, written without braces on purpose — see
      the WARNING at the end of the next comment block):
        posts-tabs layoutRhythm="true" itemContent="outside" --}}
{{!--

      WHICH POSTS EACH TAB PULLS — filterFeatured / filterExperimental,
      optional, one per tab. Each takes a COMPLETE Ghost filter string and
      defaults to the value that tab has always used, so every existing
      call site is unaffected:
        filterFeatured      "featured:true+tag:hash-work+tag:featured"
        filterExperimental  "featured:true+tag:hash-work+tag:experimental"

      Examples (call-site syntax, written without braces on purpose — see
      the WARNING at the end of this comment):
        lab posts in the first tab:
          posts-tabs filterFeatured="featured:true+tag:hash-work+tag:experimental"
        BOTH tags in one tab (comma = OR in Ghost's filter syntax):
          posts-tabs filterFeatured="featured:true+tag:hash-work+tag:[featured,experimental]"
        everything under #work, no sub-tag at all:
          posts-tabs filterFeatured="featured:true+tag:hash-work"

      A whole filter string is the parameter, rather than just a tag name,
      because Handlebars cannot concatenate: there is no way to build
      "…+tag:" + yourTag inside a template, and Ghost themes cannot register
      custom helpers to do it. The get helper DOES accept a variable for its
      filter argument,
      so passing the finished string is the one mechanism that works — at
      the cost of repeating the shared prefix at the call site.

      Filter syntax reminder (Ghost NQL): + is AND, , is OR, and [a,b]
      groups an OR of values for one field. So `tag:[featured,experimental]`
      means "either tag", while `tag:featured+tag:experimental` would demand
      BOTH on the same post.

      WARNING — do not write partial calls or helper tags with real braces
      anywhere in this comment. Handlebars ends a comment at the FIRST
      closing marker it meets, so a nested comment inside this block would
      terminate it early and everything after would be parsed as live
      template code — a partial call here would then recurse into this same
      file. That exact class of bug (helper syntax quoted inside a comment)
      already took the whole site down once, returning 400 on every route. --}}
<section class="posts-tabs-section" id="work" data-page-width="{{@custom.page_width}}" data-active-tab="featured">



  <div class="posts-tabs-wrapper">
    {{!-- Tabs header (hidden — switch component used instead) --}}
    <div class="posts-tabs-header" style="display:none">
      <div class="posts-tabs-buttons">
        <button class="posts-tab posts-tab-featured active h2" data-tab="featured" data-animate="word">Work</button>
        <button class="posts-tab posts-tab-experimental h2ac" data-tab="experimental" data-animate="word">Lab</button>
      </div>
      <p class="posts-tabs-description">Real products, real constraints, real impact.</p>
    </div>


    {{!-- Tabs content --}}
    <div class="posts-tabs-container">
      {{!-- Featured tab --}}
      <div class="posts-tabs-content posts-tabs-content-featured active" data-tab="featured">
        <div class="posts-grid"
          data-posts-layout="{{#if layoutCinematic}}cinematic{{else}}{{#if layoutGrid}}cinematic-grid{{else}}{{#if layoutRhythm}}{{#if itemContent}}grid{{else}}cinematic-rhythm{{/if}}{{else}}{{#if layoutList}}list{{else}}{{@custom.posts_layout}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}"
          {{#if layoutList}}{{#unless itemContent}}data-item-content="inside"{{/unless}}{{else}}{{#if itemContent}}{{#unless layoutRhythm}}data-item-content="outside"{{/unless}}{{/if}}{{/if}}>
          <div class="container">
            <div id="work-cards"></div>
            <div class="carousel-track">
              {{!-- filterFeatured (see this file's own doc at the top) —
                    the if-branch is what supplies the default: a get with
                    an undefined filter variable would fetch EVERY post, not
                    fall back, so the literal has to be spelled out here. --}}
              {{#if filterFeatured}}
              {{#get "posts" filter=filterFeatured limit="100" include="tags,authors"}}
                {{#foreach posts}}
                  {{> post-card first=@first}}
                {{/foreach}}
              {{/get}}
              {{else}}
              {{#get "posts" filter="featured:true+tag:hash-work+tag:featured" limit="100" include="tags,authors"}}
                {{#foreach posts}}
                  {{> post-card first=@first}}
                {{/foreach}}
              {{/get}}
              {{/if}}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-controls">
            <button class="carousel-arrow carousel-prev" aria-label="Previous post" type="button">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <button class="carousel-arrow carousel-next" aria-label="Next post" type="button">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {{!-- Experimental tab --}}
      <div class="posts-tabs-content posts-tabs-content-experimental" data-tab="experimental">
        <div class="posts-grid"
          data-posts-layout="{{#if layoutCinematic}}cinematic{{else}}{{#if layoutGrid}}cinematic-grid{{else}}{{#if layoutRhythm}}{{#if itemContent}}grid{{else}}cinematic-rhythm{{/if}}{{else}}{{#if layoutList}}list{{else}}{{@custom.posts_layout}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}"
          {{#if layoutList}}{{#unless itemContent}}data-item-content="inside"{{/unless}}{{else}}{{#if itemContent}}{{#unless layoutRhythm}}data-item-content="outside"{{/unless}}{{/if}}{{/if}}>
          <div class="container">
            <div id="work-cards"></div>
            <div class="carousel-track">
              {{!-- filterExperimental — same default-via-if-branch pattern as
                    the featured tab above; see this file's doc at the top. --}}
              {{#if filterExperimental}}
              {{#get "posts" filter=filterExperimental limit="100" include="tags,authors"}}
                {{#foreach posts}}
                  {{> post-card first=@first}}
                {{/foreach}}
              {{/get}}
              {{else}}
              {{#get "posts" filter="featured:true+tag:hash-work+tag:experimental" limit="100" include="tags,authors"}}
                {{#foreach posts}}
                  {{> post-card first=@first}}
                {{/foreach}}
              {{/get}}
              {{/if}}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-controls">
            <button class="carousel-arrow carousel-prev" aria-label="Previous post" type="button">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <button class="carousel-arrow carousel-next" aria-label="Next post" type="button">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
